      "id": 1,
      "text": "Elmwood Park is a small village nestled between the City of Racine and the Town of Mount Pleasant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.elmwoodparkwi.gov/1211/Village-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Taylor Avenue in Elmwood Park was originally called the Racine and Wilmot Plank Road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.elmwoodparkwi.gov/1211/Village-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Taylor Avenue was named after Isaac Taylor and the Taylor Children's Orphan Asylum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.elmwoodparkwi.gov/1211/Village-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Beebe School's history in Elmwood Park traces back almost to the beginning of Racine.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.elmwoodparkwi.gov/1211/Village-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "An influx of people during the 1950s eventually led to the creation of the village of Elmwood Park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.elmwoodparkwi.gov/1211/Village-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Early village meetings in Elmwood Park were conducted in the homes and garages of local residents.",
